Installing inspect_ranges registers the range sandbox provider with Inspect. A task that names it gets a freshly booted range per sample: the attacker box (or foothold host) is the sample’s sandbox, and the whole range is torn down when the sample ends. By default only the foothold is registered, so the agent’s tool loop cannot reach targets by name; targets are reachable solely through the range network. See Challenges for why that wall exists.
from inspect_ai import Task, task
from inspect_ai.dataset import Sample

@task
def my_task() -&gt; Task:
    return Task(
        dataset=[Sample(input="Recover the flag from the web host.")],
        solver=my_solver(),
        sandbox=("range", "range.yaml"),
    )
Before the first eval on a machine, derive a golden image and check the host (see Running Ranges): inspect-ranges doctor verifies the host end to end, and inspect-ranges images derive bakes the guest control daemon into a golden the range definition references.

